Package: open-transcribe-assistant
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: OpenTranscribe contributors <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/fbossiere/open-transcribe-mcp
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, ca-certificates
Recommends: gnome-keyring | kwalletmanager, xdg-utils
Description: OpenTranscribe Setup, a configuration assistant for speech-to-text over MCP
 OpenTranscribe Setup configures the OpenTranscribe transcription engine and connects it to
 a local MCP client. It bundles its own Python runtime and the engine, so no development tools
 are needed to install or run it.
 .
 Audio is sent to the transcription provider you choose, using your own provider key, which is
 stored in your session keyring. The transcript is returned to your assistant. No transcript
 history is kept by default, and no OpenTranscribe account is required.
 .
 A working Secret Service keyring in a normal graphical session is a prerequisite for setup.
 Recommending gnome-keyring does not by itself prove that a session exposes a usable keyring.
